    {
      "id": "open_session_channels",
      "operator": "client.session_channel.open_all",
      "operator_version": "0.1",
      "notes": "Each per-session open demand settles once as admitted, rejected, or cancelled. Construct the mux-channel-open from that session's runtime host. An exact target includes backend, opaque expectedSessionIdentity, and existingOnly=true. Invalid exact intent retires only its current opening row without open/close wire traffic; mux-ready still establishes physical readiness and opens healthy siblings. Cancellation retires the attempt before replacement/removal. A new exact attempt on an existing JS-owned socket uses a fresh routing ID; replacement atomically removes the old reverse lookup. Service-owned replay and legacy IDs remain unchanged. Sending keeps the channel opening. Only a current-channel opened ACK with matching stableId admits allocation and body subscription; admission is not connected/first-body readiness. Missing/mismatched ACK retires only that channel through local failure/close. On a recoverable logical close, first settle any existing pending open. For a settled current exact channel, keep the channelId/state guard and teardown, keep no_body_demand idle, and use the existing per-session host reconnect builder with the unchanged expectedSessionIdentity and existingOnly=true. A valid current exact identity makes the default name catalog irrelevant; only active/live demand schedules that reopen. A rejected original identity settles through the existing pending-intent failure terminal without name fallback, sibling admission, or input transfer. Inactive exact channels stay idle. Legacy/non-exact closes retain the existing control-status catalog branch. Old routing IDs and late closes cannot affect a newer attempt. Physical recovery remains with the target owner and re-enters through the existing open path.",
      "inputs": [
        "arc.bulk_channel_binding",
        "arc.session_demand_set",
        "arc.connection_policy"
      ],
      "output": {
        "id": "arc.session_channels",
        "schema": "Object"
      },
      "input_selector": {
        "include": [],
        "exclude": [],
        "predicate": null
      },
      "output_selector": {
        "include": [],
        "exclude": [],
        "predicate": null
      },
      "iterator": "Whole"
    },
    {
      "id": "subscribe_session_bodies",
      "operator": "client.session_channel.subscribe_bodies",
      "operator_version": "0.1",
      "notes": "Consume only channels admitted by open_session_channels. A matching exact-channel allocation may send the existing body subscription and control before terminal connected. For the JS owner-local terminal-connected input policy, only that current admitted channel's connected enables input; buffer-head, buffer-sync, UI state and mux-ready do not. New attempts, retirement and physical replacement clear readiness. A rejected, cancelled, retired, or late reply path must not subscribe or dispatch body traffic. Default exact tmux/Herdr input behavior remains unchanged; typed Rex Host wiring belongs to combination.",
      "inputs": [
        "arc.session_channels",
        "arc.session_demand_set"
      ],
